Actually let me think. The requirement says "the bounce must apply exactly once (`vy = -vy` applied twice cancels out and the ball goes through)". So if we filter/sweep and only bounce against the single best-matching brick, we avoid double-bounce. We still need to kill both collided bricks though? The issue says "every seam overlaps two bricks in the same pass". If we kill both bricks that's fine for gameplay. We destroy all collided bricks but only bounce once.

